# Lab rules for UFW on linux-srv (lab/wazuh/manager/local_rules.xml).
# Sample lines are made up, in Ubuntu 24.04's journald format.

[UFW block is decoded and alerted]
log: Oct 11 21:40:01 linux-srv kernel: [UFW BLOCK] IN=eth0 OUT= MAC=00:0c:29:aa:bb:cc:00:0c:29:dd:ee:ff:08:00 SRC=10.0.1.10 DST=10.0.1.30 LEN=60 TOS=0x00 PREC=0x00 TTL=64 ID=54321 DF PROTO=TCP SPT=51515 DPT=3306 WINDOW=64240 RES=0x00 SYN URGP=0
rule: 100100
level: 5
field: srcip=10.0.1.10
field: dstport=3306

[six blocks stay under the port-scan threshold]
log: Oct 11 21:40:01 linux-srv kernel: [UFW BLOCK] IN=eth0 OUT= MAC=00:0c:29:aa:bb:cc:00:0c:29:dd:ee:ff:08:00 SRC=10.0.1.10 DST=10.0.1.30 LEN=60 TOS=0x00 PREC=0x00 TTL=64 ID=54321 DF PROTO=TCP SPT=51515 DPT=3306 WINDOW=64240 RES=0x00 SYN URGP=0
repeat: 6
rule: 100100

[eight blocks from one source in a minute look like a scan]
log: Oct 11 21:40:01 linux-srv kernel: [UFW BLOCK] IN=eth0 OUT= MAC=00:0c:29:aa:bb:cc:00:0c:29:dd:ee:ff:08:00 SRC=10.0.1.10 DST=10.0.1.30 LEN=60 TOS=0x00 PREC=0x00 TTL=64 ID=54321 DF PROTO=TCP SPT=51515 DPT=3306 WINDOW=64240 RES=0x00 SYN URGP=0
repeat: 8
rule: 100102
level: 10
